    out (Tensor, optional): the output tensor.

Example::

    >>> t = torch.randn(3, 4)
    >>> t
    tensor([[-0.1321,  0.4370, -1.2631, -1.1289],
            [-2.0527, -1.1250,  0.2275,  0.3077],
            [-0.0881, -0.1259, -0.5495,  1.0284]])
    >>> torch.msort(t)
    tensor([[-2.0527, -1.1250, -1.2631, -1.1289],
            [-0.1321, -0.1259, -0.5495,  0.3077],
